        "subject": "LU-20730 llapi: read and write LFU Object Stream chunks",
        "message": "LU-20730 llapi: read and write LFU Object Stream chunks\n\nA scan hands its consumer one struct llapi_scan_rec per callback.\nThe record holds pointers and file descriptors, so it cannot leave\nthe process, and a consumer that wants many objects at once has to\nbatch them itself. The LFU Object Stream fixes that format: a bulk of\nfixed-size slots, each holding one Cap'n Proto LfuChunk message with\na list of LfuInode records and their EA values, defined in\nlfu.capnp by Timothy Day.\n\nAdd lfu.capnp to include/uapi/linux/lustre, installed beside the\nheaders, and lustre_lfu_capnp.h with its enum values and the field\noffsets the schema compiles to, so C needs no Cap'n Proto compiler.\n\nAdd liblustreapi_lfu.c, a codec for the part the Lustre producers\nsend: LfuChunk with an empty or inodes union, LfuInode, LfuEa and the\nskipped list. The writer lays a chunk out in place, records from the\nfront and EA values from the back, and writes the list headers last,\nso no batch is staged. It is internal (lustreapi_lfu.h) until a\nproducer uses it, and is built as liblfu_codec.la, linked into\nliblustreapi and into the test. The reader is public:\nllapi_lfu_chunk_parse(), llapi_lfu_chunk_inode() and\nllapi_lfu_chunk_skipped(). It reads in place and trusts nothing: every\npointer is checked against the segment, far pointers and zero-sized\nstruct lists are refused, and a struct shorter than the schema reads\nas zero past its end.\n\nllapi_lfu_test, run by sanity 56En, checks a chunk written by libcapnp\n(pycapnp 2.2.4), a round trip over 16 slots, a record too large for\nits slot and a jumbo chunk, a chunk of skipped objects only, refused\ninput, and every one-bit corruption of a chunk's first KiB. The bulk\nthe round trip writes (\"-w FILE\") decodes with libcapnp too.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Artem Blagodarenko <ablagodarenko@thelustrecollective.com>\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I2c5c9177f4446c10ddd962d1bb35f5c2bc846fe1\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
